{"name":"Berkeley Hills","hex":"#7e613f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hills","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of hill","A region in which there are many hills; a hilly area."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of hill"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hills"}],"entries":[{"title":"Berkeley Hills","blocks":[{"text":"The Berkeley Hills are a range of the Pacific Coast Ranges, and overlook the northeast side of the valley that encompasses San Francisco Bay. They were previously called the \"Contra Costa Range/Hills\", but with the establishment of Berkeley and the University of California, the name was updated by geographers and gazetteers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Grizzly_Bench.jpg/330px-Grizzly_Bench.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkeley_Hills","wikidata":"Q4892037"},{"title":"Hill","blocks":[{"text":"A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG/330px-Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill","wikidata":"Q54050"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Berkeley_Hills_Orinda.jpg/500px-Berkeley_Hills_Orinda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Berkeley_Hills_Orinda.jpg/1280px-Berkeley_Hills_Orinda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://th